course: dictionary
lesson: 8276
title: Rind: the tough outer skin
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rind is the thick, tough outer layer of some foods, such as oranges, lemons and watermelons. It can also be the hard outer layer of cheese or bacon. Its job is to protect what is inside. «He packs bananas, sugar-cane and melons, says goodbye, and walks across Africa, dropping melon rind all the way» shows the rind being left behind after the fruit is eaten.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Dropping melon rind and throwing the rind about tell you that a rind is something you throw away. Cooking gives another clue: lemon rind gives flavour to cakes, so it is something people also use. Now swap in your meaning: "He dropped the thick outer skin of the melon all the way" still makes sense, so your guess is right.
explain: Rind has an old meaning too: the bark of a tree. This is an old use, so you will not see it often today. When a word has more than one meaning, the sentence tells you which meaning the author wants.
fact: A rind is the thick, tough outer skin of some fruits, like oranges, lemons and watermelons.
fact: The hard outer layer of cheese or bacon is also called a rind, as in «cheese rind» and «bacon rind».
fact: In old use, rind can mean the bark of a tree.
fact: Lemon rind, when grated, is called zest, and it gives flavour to cakes.
fact: A rind protects the fruit or food inside it.
exercise: What does rind mean? | A long, thin leaf on a tree | A kind of brass band instrument | The soft, sweet juice inside a fruit | *The thick, tough outer skin of some fruits
exercise: «You cut the rind off the bacon before you eat it.» Which thing is the rind? | The soft meat inside the bacon | *The hard outer layer of the bacon | The slice of bacon you eat | The pan you cook the bacon in
exercise: Find the word in «Lemon rind gives flavour to cakes.» that means the skin of the lemon. | lemon | cakes | *rind | flavour
test: What is lemon rind called when it is grated? | pulp | *zest | pips | juice
test: «Going home, he picked up the melon rind he had dropped, for he was a Tidy Pachyderm.» What does pachyderm mean? | *A thick-skinned animal | A tidy friend who keeps things clean | A kind of fruit | The bark of a tree
exam: What does «cheese rind» mean? | A hole in the cheese | The soft middle of the cheese | A shop that sells cheese | *The hard outer layer of the cheese
